.nh
.TH "TEAMS" "1" "Oct 2026" "teams dev" "teams Manual"

.SH NAME
teams-search - Search Teams messages


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBteams search  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Search Teams messages with KQL. The documented scope terms are available
through flags (--from, --to, --mentions-me, --has-attachment) and inline in
, so from:bob sent>2026-10-01 keeps working.

.PP
A hit carries no message body: Graph returns the id, the sender, the
timestamps, the subject and a web link (docs/spike/phase1.md:83).
Use \fBteams thread read <link>\fR for the text.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--from\fP=""
	only messages sent by this person (from:)

.PP
\fB--has-attachment\fP[=false]
	only messages with attachments

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for search

.PP
\fB--in\fP=""
	only messages in this channel or chat

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=25
	results per page (the API allows up to 50)

.PP
\fB--mentions-me\fP[=false]
	only messages that mention you

.PP
\fB--page\fP=1
	1-based page number (the search API pages by from/size)

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	only messages newer than this (a duration like 7d, or a timestamp)

.PP
\fB--to\fP=""
	only messages sent to this person (to:, 1:1 chats only)

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	only messages older than this (a duration like 7d, or a timestamp)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--jq\fP=""
	filter JSON output through a jq expression (implies --json)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also honours NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-input\fP[=false]
	never prompt; fail fast instead

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (default: the configured default_profile)

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress progress messages on stderr

.PP
\fB--read-only\fP[=false]
	refuse write commands

.PP
\fB--refresh\fP[=false]
	ignore cached names and resolve them again

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	verbose diagnostics on stderr (-v, -vv)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBteams(1)\fP
